    "title": "老 + predicate",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk4-time-p15-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "老 + predicate",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "老 before a predicate can describe persistent recurrence, often with frustration. It does not describe age in this use.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他老迟到。",
                "pinyin": "tā lǎo chídào 。",
                "meaning": "He keeps arriving late.",
                "audio": "ff27b068b3e1b5f9d9d673411aecb5993da595dd3096e2273a18000524ccd0a6"
              },
              {
                "text": "你怎么老问这个问题？",
                "pinyin": "nǐ zěnme lǎo wèn zhè gè wèntí ？",
                "meaning": "Why do you keep asking this question?",
                "audio": "c898cb4e1f6cc3f36ae8e74239ea931bd80dc98bcd012011182976f8e6b2d0f5"
              }
            ]
          },
